                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]The Last Dream[/b] tells the story of a tragically separated couple struggling to reunite . . .  which was not really my cup of tea. That being said, the story was well told and the full motion video scenes were used to good effect. \n\nI've played a number of Hidden Object Games, but this was my first FRagmented Object Game. It's a fun variation where you search a scene for pieces of an object that, when assembled, helps you find more objects. The mini games were variations of familiar favourites. The collectibles were well hidden but not impossible to find. There are fun extras to this edition by way of wallpapers and a Bonus Chapter. I enjoyed playing this game. \n\nI purchased this title as part of a bundle offered by the developer, so yes - value for money spent.\nRecommended.",
